<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1">
  <DUT Name="ST_Permissive_HMI_Interface" Id="{84f28cf2-22c5-4efc-88d5-aafb1a2049ad}">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[// HMI face of fb_Permissive. Bind <instance>.HMI.* — the shared lhmi `PermissiveList` component
// renders exactly this struct, so any permissive anywhere (a device's start conditions, a
// MachineFlow transition gate, a machine-level ready check) gets the same operator view for free.
//
// There is deliberately NO first-out field here. First-out answers "which condition dropped and
// caused the trip", which only means something for an interlock: it faults instantly, so the
// condition that went first is the cause and the later ones are consequences. A permissive never
// trips - it is evaluated at the moment something asks to proceed, and every unmet condition is
// equally and simultaneously the reason. So this struct carries the SET (stsConditions) plus a
// count, and the HMI shows all of them rather than nominating a misleading headline.
//
// There is deliberately NO BYPASS field either. A permissive is not a safety function, so the
// temptation is to say a bypass is harmless here — but it is the one control that can make an
// unsatisfied gate report itself satisfied, and a sequence that advances on a forced permissive
// fails somewhere downstream where nothing explains why. Hold the conditions or do not; there is
// no third answer to publish. (fb_Interlock's inpGlobalBypass is a different case: an interlock
// stops a running machine, so commissioning needs a documented way to move it.)
//
// Bounds are literals, per CONVENTIONS §5 — matched to ST_Permissive's ten slots. Plain STRING is
// STRING(80), the same width the descriptions carry there.
TYPE ST_Permissive_HMI_Interface :
STRUCT
    stsPermissiveOK     : BOOL;     // TRUE when every condition is met
    stsConditions       : ARRAY[1..10] OF BOOL;
    stsDescriptions     : ARRAY[1..10] OF STRING;
    stsUnmetCount       : INT;      // how many are unmet — 0 when satisfied
    stsPermissiveName   : STRING;   // set via the cfgName property
END_STRUCT
END_TYPE
]]></Declaration>
  </DUT>
</TcPlcObject>
